# .gitignore — Git ignore backstop for MANIFEST.json exclusions (D-07/D-08/D-10/D-14/D-15)
#
# Second layer ONLY: the primary structural denylist lives in MANIFEST.json
# (`excludes` per entry) and is consumed by capture (Phase 2). These rules stop
# ordinary `git add` of untracked sensitive/generated paths.
#
# Recursive `**/` patterns below cover every managed root mirrored under home/.
# Package manifests and lockfiles stay versioned (`npm ci` rebuilds modules).

# --- secrets & credentials (never versioned) ---
**/jev.env
**/.git-credentials
**/.claude.json
*.env
*.pem
*.key
**/BEGIN *PRIVATE KEY*
**/*token*
**/*secret*

# --- generated / reinstallable (rebuilt by `npm ci`) ---
**/node_modules/
**/bin/
dist/
build/

# --- archives & backup leftovers (never versioned) ---
**/*.tar.gz
**/*.tgz
**/*.tar
**/*.zip
**/*.bak*
**/*.bak-*
**/*.backup-*
**/opencode-backup/
**/opencode-backup-*.tar.gz
**/agents.bak-*
*backup-*
legacy-archive/
.opencode-ecosystem-backup/

# --- machine-local (never overwritten by restore, never committed) ---
**/*.local
home/.azure

# --- GSD ephemeral ---
.planning/.gsd-state-tmp/
